---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Admin
    participant Page as Admin site page<br/>SIR list
    participant Server as Server actions<br/>InspectionQueries
    participant DB as Supabase DB<br/>W26_form_responses, W26_answers,<br/>W26_attachments
    participant S3 as AWS S3

    Note over Admin,S3: Covers US 7.0.8. Deactivate exists (setFormResponseActive). Delete does not.<br/>"(proposed)" = the step is not in the code today.

    Admin->>Page: Select Delete on a SIR (proposed)
    Page-->>Admin: Ask to confirm, with the number of answers and images (AT 1)
    Admin->>Page: Confirm
    Page->>Server: deleteFormResponse(responseId) (proposed)
    Server->>Server: Check caller is Admin from a trusted role source
    alt Caller is not Admin (AT 4)
        Server-->>Page: Refused. The SIR stays unchanged
        Note over Admin,Server: A Steward who sends the request directly is refused the same way
    else Caller is Admin
        Server->>DB: Read storage_key of each W26_attachments row of the SIR
        Server->>DB: One transaction (database function, proposed):<br/>delete attachments, answers, then the response
        alt Transaction fails (AT 5)
            DB-->>Server: Error. Rollback
            Server-->>Page: Error. The SIR and its answers stay unchanged
        else Transaction succeeds
            DB-->>Server: OK
            Server->>S3: Delete each image file (proposed)
            Note over DB,S3: If an S3 delete fails, the row is already gone.<br/>Log the key for a later cleanup.
            Server-->>Page: Deleted
            Page-->>Admin: SIR is gone from the Site and report lists. Its images are not shown (AT 2, AT 3)
        end
    end

    Note over Admin,S3: Open question: the client must say how delete is different from deactivate.<br/>Deactivate hides the SIR and keeps its files (US 7.0.5 AT 4). Delete removes it.<br/>Today rollbackSiteInspectionSubmission deletes rows with separate calls and no transaction.
